# Line endings for scripts: stored and checked out with LF on every OS, so a clone on Windows still
# runs its bash and Python (a CRLF shebang fails with "bad interpreter"); Windows command files keep CRLF.
# No "* text=auto" rule: some upstream copies in third-party/ and ports/ are committed with CRLF and
# their checksums in SOURCE.md must not change.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.bat   text eol=crlf
